                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States Government to William Anderson,
                        Saxon &amp; Co., Dr.</hi> 1863.</head>
                <p>November 23.—To 250 tons coal taken from Penguin island, by the boats and crew of
                    the United States steamer Vanderbilt, by order of Captain Baldwin, on the 31st
                    of October last, at £6 per ton £1,500</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cape Town.</hi></p>
